      },
      "worked": "The midpoint is\n$$\\begin{align*}M&=\\left(\\frac{-1+5}{2},\\frac{4+8}{2}\\right)\\\\M&=(2,6).\\end{align*}$$\nThe gradient of $PQ$ is\n$$\\begin{align*}m_{PQ}&=\\frac{8-4}{5-(-1)}\\\\m_{PQ}&=\\frac{2}{3}.\\end{align*}$$\nPerpendicular gradients have product $-1$, so\n$$\\begin{align*}m_{\\perp}&=-\\frac{1}{2/3}\\\\m_{\\perp}&=-\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{align*}$$\nUsing point–gradient form through $(2,6)$:\n$$\\begin{align*}y-6&=-\\frac{3}{2}(x-2)\\\\2y-12&=-3x+6\\\\3x+2y-18&=0.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
